      "lineNbr": 26,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-07T09:42:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Traditionally we\u0027ve avoided exposing raw netIds in any sort of API because doing so would preclude us from changing the implementation of the Network class to something else. That\u0027s why we added the network handle. See Network#getNetworkHandle.\n\nIn this case, though, given that the bulk of the code that understands netIds is in the non-updatable system, and the module is presumed newer than the system, it\u0027s probably fine to use a netId here: once the system is upgraded, we\u0027ll be able to upgrade the module as well.\n\nAnother option would be to make a ParcelableNetwork class and have Network contain a ParcelableNetwork instead of an int.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 26,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 26,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "cf4d8198e22f1c30d8b1c700bd8f88c31e1810bf",
